-- The W1 fixture's second shape (BLAWX-EXPORT-SPEC §11 W1, §4.1), measured
-- 2026-09-02: record identity smuggled inside a CONTAINER.
--
-- `not-ok/record-identity.l4` compares two Player records directly. This file
-- never mentions a bare Player on either side of an `EQUALS` — it compares two
-- `LIST OF Player` fields, and then two `LIST OF MAYBE Player` fields — and it
-- diverges for exactly the same reason. L4 compares a list element-wise BY
-- VALUE; Blawx unifies it element-wise BY ATOM; and R11's flattening still
-- mints one object per OCCURRENCE, so a roster and its structural twin arrive
-- as lists of different atoms.
--
-- Measured before the refusal descended into containers: `l4 blawx` on the
-- first rule exited 0 and emitted `Members = Members2` inside
-- `according_to(sec_1_section,same_roster,A,B)`. The refusal now covers any
-- operand sort that CONTAINS a declared record, under any nesting of `LIST OF`
-- and `MAYBE`, which is why both rules below are rejected and why this file
-- carries the `MAYBE` one: a bare `MAYBE Player` FIELD is refused earlier, by
-- the ontology check ("sort with no Blawx value type"), so `LIST OF MAYBE
-- Player` is the only reachable way to put a `MAYBE` under this check.
--
-- The edits that work are the same two the diagnostic names: state the rule
-- once per slot, or compare fields whose sorts are atoms.

§ `Roster Identity`

DECLARE Player HAS
    number IS A NUMBER

DECLARE Team HAS
    members IS A LIST OF Player
    reserves IS A LIST OF MAYBE Player

@export A team fields the same roster as another if their member lists are the same.
GIVEN a IS A Team
      b IS A Team
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `same roster` a b IF
  a's members EQUALS b's members

@export A team keeps the same reserves as another if their reserve lists are the same.
GIVEN a IS A Team
      b IS A Team
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `same reserves` a b IF
  a's reserves EQUALS b's reserves
